# Build context exclusions. All three Dockerfiles build from the repo root and use
# blanket `COPY <dir> ./`, so anything left here is baked into an image layer.
#
# The worker env files are the reason this file exists: .env.live holds live R2 and
# database credentials, and `COPY services/worker ./` would otherwise bake them into
# the image. The worker gets its config from the environment at run time
# (docker-compose / Render), so it never needs these files inside the image.
services/worker/.env
services/worker/.env.live

# Do NOT broaden this to a blanket `**/.env`: the web image runs `vite build` inside
# Docker, and Vite reads apps/web/.env at build time for the VITE_* vars. Excluding
# it would silently strip them from the built bundle.

services/worker/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
